WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.330
Film Courage: Eli how did you know you were
a filmmaker and not a film watcher?

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.950
Elias Daughdrill, Long Beach City College
Film Professor and Writer/Director: That’s

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:05.950
a really good question.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:08.860
So that was the kind of thing I was going
through at San Francisco State University

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.690
that maybe I don’t know enough about this
technology?

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.120
Maybe I should go on and get a PhD?

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:18.540
Like that was something I was seriously considering.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:28.460
But for whatever reason I don’t know how
you know other than you keep having the drive

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.710
to make something.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.690
I think that is probably the test.

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:37.680
One of the things I tell the students, they
kind of don’t know that they are getting

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.460
themselves into for the first time even if
they make just a short film.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:46.360
So when it’s all over they’re stressed
out and they feel like their movie is not

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:52.310
as good as it could have been or it’s not
what they wanted to make because it’s a

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:53.760
movie.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:59.430
And I tell them that the test is though you
went through all of that stress, it was incredibly

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:07.430
hectic, you ultimately feel like the film
could be better which is what everybody thinks

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:12.760
after they make a movie, so you’re not a
100% happy with the finished product.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:18.330
But the test is if you wake up in a couple
of days, a couple of weeks, a couple of months

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:23.830
AND you want to make something again then
you want to be a filmmaker.

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:29.570
So the drive to Oh...I’m interested in this.

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:36.990
I’m interested in using the camera to try
to get at ideas or tell stories or project

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:46.910
some perspective of the world if that doesn’t
go away and it hasn’t gone away yet, that’s

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:47.910
how I knew.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:53.341
But there was a question in those moments
like I was describing where oh my gosh, they

00:01:53.341 --> 00:01:55.950
all know more than I do.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:03.440
And there is something about just filmmaking
because it’s just so heavily titled toward

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:13.140
men or guys and they are so full of (can be...not
all guys) can be full of bravado and trying

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.910
to prove themselves.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:20.920
Film sets are so full of guys trying to prove
how much they know, what they’ve done, so

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:23.060
that can be really intimidating like “Oh?

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.790
I don’t know as much as these guys.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:28.790
They’re talking about a lens that I don’t
know anything about or they are talking about

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:32.950
a camera or they are talking about something
with a dolly shot that I don’t know anything

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:33.950
about.”

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:40.080
So that can make you go “Okay, I’ll just
be the guy who...maybe I’ll write reviews

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.510
or whatever.

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:51.060
Or I’ll do a dissertation on Mike Lee films
because I love Mike Lee or whatever.”

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.060
But then...”Oh?

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:54.370
This is an idea.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:57.520
I should write that down and you start writing
something.”

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:06.350
The great thing about if you are a...like
me, I consider myself a writer/director.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:12.080
I write my own stuff and I make it, nobody
can stop me...there’s nothing stopping me

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:14.670
from writing a script.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:22.690
That doesn’t cost any money, it’s just
my time and if I’m enjoying it and I feel

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:28.150
like it is interesting and I can turn it into
something and I can just do that and then

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:31.319
I can make a decision whether or not I want
to try and make it.

00:03:31.319 --> 00:03:37.810
I don’t know, that still holds a lot of
pleasure for me.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:42.870
If it stops, if it’s not pleasureful anymore,
then I’ll stop doing it because filmmaking

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:43.930
is too hard.

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:48.091
It’s way too hard to do something you are
not getting anything out of it.

00:03:48.091 --> 00:03:54.769
It doesn’t feel fun or if you don’t feel
like you are doing anything interesting.

